.Dd August 3, 2026
.Dt ROOK-PLUGIN 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rook-plugin
.Nd rook's plugin protocol
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A rook plugin is a separate process speaking newline-delimited JSON over
its own stdin and stdout.
rook spawns it, asks it questions
.Pq Cm items.list , Cm items.act ,
renders its answers in the side panel, and lets it ask two things back
.Pq Cm attention.raise , Cm session.spawn .
Every operation, in both directions, is gated by
.Em grants
declared in the configuration \(em a plugin can do exactly what its
declaration says and nothing else.
.Pp
Anything a plugin can be: a shell script, a Go binary, anything that reads
lines and writes lines.
The canonical minimal plugin,
.Pa examples/hello-plugin
in the rook repository, is 1.3 KB of POSIX sh.
.Sh DECLARING
A plugin is a node in the environment graph
.Pq see Xr rook-config 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{"id": "plugin.hello", "kind": "plugin", "name": "hello",
 "command": ["/path/to/hello-plugin"],
 "load": "lazy", "grants": ["items.list", "attention.raise"]}
.Ed
.Bl -tag -width "command" -offset indent
.It Cm name
Required.
The registry key, and the cache filename for sourced plugins.
.It Cm command
Argv of a binary already on disk.
.It Cm source
A URL to fetch the binary from
.Pq Ql https:// No or Ql file:// .
Mutually exclusive with
.Cm command .
.It Cm sha256
The pin: lowercase hex digest the downloaded binary must match.
.It Cm load
.Ql eager
.Pq spawn at launch
or
.Ql lazy
.Pq spawn on first use; the default .
.It Cm grants
The ops this plugin may be asked, and may ask \(em by name, both
directions.
.El
.Pp
SDK spellings:
.Ql e.Plugin(name, argv, load, grants...) ,
.Ql e.PluginFrom(source, grants...) ,
.Ql e.PluginPinned(source, sha256, grants...) .
.Sh LIFECYCLE
For a
.Cm source
plugin, first use downloads via curl to
.Pa <cache>/<name>.part
and renames into place
.Pq an interrupted fetch cannot leave a half binary that looks present ;
the cache is
.Pa $XDG_DATA_HOME/rook/plugins/ ,
default
.Pa ~/.local/share/rook/plugins/ .
.Pp
The binary is verified on
.Em every
launch, not only after download:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent -compact
.It
With a
.Cm sha256
pin: mismatch is refusal.
.It
Without one: trust-on-first-use \(em the first hash is recorded in a
.Pa .sha256
sidecar, and a later change is refusal
.Pq Dq changed since it was downloaded \(em delete it to accept the new one .
.It
A refusal never re-downloads.
The plugin is marked failed, its reason readable via
.Ql ctl plugins
and in the panel.
.El
.Pp
rook offers the pin rather than making you compute it: while a sourced
plugin is up and unpinned,
.Ql ctl plugins
prints its
.Ql sha256= ,
and
.Ql y
in the plugin panel copies a ready-to-paste
.Ql PluginPinned(...)
line
.Em in the language your config program is written in .
.Pp
A spawned plugin's stderr goes to
.Pa /dev/null ;
a plugin that fails stays failed until relaunch.
The failure is a row in
.Ql ctl plugins ,
never a crash of rook.
.Sh THE PROTOCOL
Version 1.
One JSON object per line, at most 1 MiB.
Requests from rook:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{"v":1,"id":7,"op":"items.list","deadlineMs":9750,
 "params":{"root":"/path/to/repo","limit":128}}
.Ed
.Pp
Replies carry the same
.Cm id :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{"v":1,"id":7,"ok":true,"result":{...}}
{"v":1,"id":7,"ok":false,"error":"why"}
.Ed
.Pp
Answer within
.Cm deadlineMs
.Pq rook waits 10 s by default and gives you that minus a grace .
Frames from the plugin
.Em with
an
.Ql op
field are requests to rook; without one they are replies.
That is the whole framing rule, and it is what lets a plugin raise an
attention in the middle of answering a call.
.Ss Operations rook sends
.Bl -tag -width "items.list"
.It Cm describe
The handshake, sent once after spawn; not grant-gated.
Reply:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{"v":1,"id":1,"ok":true,"result":{"name":"hello",
 "version":"0.1.0","capabilities":["items.list"]}}
.Ed
.Pp
A
.Ql v
other than 1 is refused outright.
.Cm capabilities
is what the plugin
.Em wants ;
grants are what it
.Em gets ;
.Ql ctl plugins
shows both so the gap is visible.
.It Cm items.list
Params:
.Ql root
.Pq the focused pane's repository root, possibly empty
and
.Ql limit .
Reply
.Ql result.items
.Pq plus Ql truncated bool :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{"id":"pr-12","title":"fix the frobnicator","state":"running",
 "subtitle":"opened 2h ago",
 "fields":[{"key":"count","kind":"NUMBER","value":"42"}],
 "actions":[{"id":"merge","label":"Merge","confirm":true}],
 "children":[...]}
.Ed
.Pp
Everything except
.Cm id
and
.Cm title
is optional.
Caps: 128 items, 6 fields and 6 actions per item, two levels deep
.Pq children of children do not render .
An action with
.Cm confirm
true gets a real y/n confirm in the panel before
.Cm items.act
is sent.
.It Cm items.act
Params:
.Ql itemId
and
.Ql actionId .
Reply
.Ql result.message
.Pq shown in the panel
and optionally
.Ql result.item ,
the updated item; omit it and rook refetches the list instead.
.It Ar anything else
.Ql ctl plugin <name> <op> [params-json]
calls any op directly, still grant-gated \(em the escape hatch for ops the
panel has no surface for yet.
.El
.Ss Operations a plugin may send
Same frame shape, plugin's own
.Cm id ;
rook answers
.Ql {"v":1,"id":N,"ok":true}
or an error.
Each requires its grant, refused by name
.Pq Ql not granted: session.spawn .
.Bl -tag -width "attention.raise"
.It Cm attention.raise
Params:
.Ql title
.Pq required
and
.Ql body .
Lands in the attention inbox
.Pq Ql ctl attention .
Provenance is server-assigned from the declaration \(em a plugin cannot
claim to be another.
.It Cm session.spawn
Params:
.Ql command
.Pq required ,
.Ql cwd
.Pq default: the focused pane's ,
.Ql where
.Pq Ql tab No for a new tab; default a split .
Opens without stealing focus.
.El
.Sh THE PANEL
Open with
.Ql <leader>p
.Pq the plugin picker
or
.Ql ctl plugin-show <name> .
.Ql j / k
move,
.Ql Enter
descends into an item's actions and runs one
.Pq through its confirm if it asks for one ,
.Ql r
refetches,
.Ql y
copies the pin line,
.Ql ESC
backs out.
In a confirm, only
.Ql y
runs and only
.Ql n
or
.Ql ESC
cancels \(em a confirm that any key dismisses is not a confirm.
.Sh A MINIMAL PLUGIN
The essence of
.Pa examples/hello-plugin ,
a sh script:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#!/bin/sh
while IFS= read -r line; do
  id=$(expr "$line" : '.*"id":\e([0-9]*\e)')
  case $line in
  *'"op":"describe"'*)
    printf '{"v":1,"id":%s,"ok":true,"result":{"name":"hello",
      "version":"0.1.0","capabilities":["items.list"]}}\en' "$id" ;;
  *'"op":"items.list"'*)
    printf '{"v":1,"id":%s,"ok":true,"result":{"items":[
      {"id":"one","title":"hello from a plugin","state":"ok"}
      ],"truncated":false}}\en' "$id" ;;
  *)
    printf '{"v":1,"id":%s,"ok":false,
      "error":"hello only does items.list"}\en' "$id" ;;
  esac
done
.Ed
.Pp
No build step, no network, no clock \(em and it exercises the whole
machinery.
Declare it, grant
.Ql items.list ,
relaunch, open the panel.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr rook 1 ,
.Xr rook-config 5 ,
.Xr rook-ctl 7
.Pp
.Pa docs/plugins/VOCABULARY.md
in the repository \(em the item model this protocol is designed against,
including the parts not yet implemented.
.Sh CAVEATS
Only the List surface renders today;
.Ql surfaces
in
.Cm describe
is accepted and ignored.
.Pp
Actions that declare an
.Cm input
are refused by name \(em rook has no form surface yet.
.Pp
The plugin set is read at launch: adding or removing a declaration takes
a relaunch.
.Pp
.Cm session.send
and
.Cm notify
appear in the vocabulary document but are not implemented.
